{{// Render here to retain variable timing; emit through the matching assembler. }}
{{#setvar::NemoAssembled_nemo_narrative_progression_swipe_correction}}{{setvar::NNPSwipeGenerationType::{{lastGenerationType}}}}{{#if {{getvar::NNPEnabled}}}}{{#if {{.NNPSwipeGenerationType == swipe}}}}
[NARRATIVE PROGRESSION: SWIPE REPLACES ONE TURN]
Use the accepted predecessor of the replaced assistant reply as the counting base, excluding the discarded reply and all its alternatives. For the same arc and stage, add one for the replacement substantive fictional reply, not one for each swipe attempt. A predecessor held count of 6 produces 7 in each same-stage replacement, never 8 or 9 because it was swiped again. An already counted endpoint of 7 is replaced by another 7; do not repeatedly subtract from it.

Apply a real transition from its cause and begin that new stage's age normally. Pure OOC adds no fictional turn; a continuation extends the same reply. Preserve unknown/approximate age rather than inventing a missing count. Do not decrement elapsed fictional time, MP state, canon, reset points, relationships, or unrelated counters. This is a rule for the existing model-maintained stage record, not a claim that the preset decremented a stored runtime counter.
