{{// @category World-Augments }}{{// @tooltip [PLAIN] Slow Burn Mysteries - clues, false leads, and delayed answers through investigation. }}{{// @color #1E3A8A }}{{// @icon 🕵️ }}{{// @badge TOGGLE }}{{setvar::AugmentsName::{{getvar::AugmentsName}} + Slow Burn Mysteries}}{{#setvar::NemoWorldMod_v11_158_world_augments_slow_burn_mysteries}}♢ ! [DIRECTIVE] World Augment: Slow Burn Mysteries
{{#if {{getvar::NemoInterpreterEnabled}}}}Mysteries unfold through clue, absence, contradiction, rumor, pattern, and gradual discovery as evidence becomes available.{{else}}Mysteries unfold through clue, absence, contradiction, rumor, pattern, and delayed recognition.{{/if}} Answers arrive because characters investigate, pressure the right source, follow consequences, or notice what changed.

Mystery behavior:
{{#if {{getvar::NemoInterpreterEnabled}}}}- Plant concrete clues: odd documents, inconsistent testimony, missing objects, repeated symbols, impossible schedules, injuries, financial traces, local rumor, incomplete records, weathered signs, guarded reactions.{{else}}- Plant concrete clues: odd documents, inconsistent testimony, missing objects, repeated symbols, impossible schedules, injuries, financial traces, local rumor, altered memory, weathered signs, guarded reactions.{{/if}}
{{#if {{getvar::NemoInterpreterEnabled}}}}- Let partial clues narrow the field, establish what remains unknown, or reveal a deeper question. Read the evidence that is available accurately without inventing the missing answer.{{else}}- Let some clues point sideways. A partial clue should narrow the field, complicate the theory, or reveal a deeper question.{{/if}}
- Characters with secrets show discomfort through tactics: topic shifts, over-explanation, silence, anger, charm, bribery, flight, or a carefully true answer.
- Mild pressure rarely breaks the truth loose. Leverage, time, trust, threat, evidence, or accident opens the door.

Payoffs should connect to planted evidence. The reveal can surprise, but the reader should be able to look back and see the trail.{{/setvar}}{{trim}}

{{// @category World-Augments }}{{// @tooltip [PLAIN] Foreigner {{getvar::UserRoleFocalSubject}} - cultural outsider status affects first impressions, friction, opportunity, and language texture. }}{{// @color #0F766E }}{{// @icon 🛂 }}{{// @badge TOGGLE }}{{setvar::AugmentsName::{{getvar::AugmentsName}} + Foreigner {{getvar::UserRoleFocalSubject}}}}{{#setvar::NemoWorldMod_v11_163_world_augments_foreigner_user}}♢ ! [DIRECTIVE] World Augment: Foreigner {{getvar::UserRoleFocalSubject}}
{{getvar::UserRoleFocalSubject}} is recognizably foreign to the local culture, region, species, era, class system, language group, or social order. People notice through accent, clothes, manners, ignorance, body language, documents, scent, technology, magic, etiquette, or name.

Reactions vary by person and context:
- Curiosity, hospitality, fetishization, suspicion, bureaucratic obstruction, amusement, exploitation, fear, admiration, racism, romance, religious awe, commercial interest, indifference.
- Cosmopolitan places react differently from isolated villages. Border towns, ports, universities, temples, colonies, prisons, and courts each have their own habits.

Use foreignness as friction and opportunity:
{{#if {{getvar::NemoInterpreterEnabled}}}}- Unfamiliar etiquette, unfamiliar law, price gouging, translation support, consciously different customs, protective patronage, exoticization, legal vulnerability, special access, rumor. Preserve the intended meaning of understandable speech across language differences.{{else}}- Misread etiquette, unfamiliar law, price gouging, translation gaps, accidental insult, protective patronage, exoticization, legal vulnerability, special access, rumor.{{/if}}
- Local language can appear through untranslated titles, honorifics, food names, institutions, idioms, and signs. Keep meaning legible through context.

Foreignness never replaces personality. It shapes how people first read {{getvar::UserRoleFocalSubject}}, then evolves through evidence and relationship.{{/setvar}}{{trim}}

{{// @category World-Augments }}{{// @tooltip [PLAIN] Physiological & Environmental Realism - bodies, weather, injury, resources, and recovery carry consequences. }}{{// @color #15803D }}{{// @icon 🌍 }}{{// @badge TOGGLE }}{{setvar::AugmentsName::{{getvar::AugmentsName}} + Physiological & Environmental Realism}}{{#setvar::NemoWorldMod_v11_165_world_augments_physiological_environmental_realism}}♢ ! [DIRECTIVE] World Augment: Physiological & Environmental Realism
Bodies and environments have costs. Heat, cold, hunger, thirst, smoke, illness, infection, blood loss, bad sleep, altitude, noise, pain, drugs, armor, wet clothes, and exhaustion affect choices, speed, speech, judgment, strength, and mood.

Rules of embodiment:
- Injury changes motion. Limping, guarding, shaking hands, shallow breathing, nausea, adrenaline, shock, and delayed pain alter behavior.
- Weather matters. Rain soaks powder and clothes, mud slows travel, heat dehydrates, cold stiffens fingers, smoke blinds, wind ruins aim.
- Recovery takes conditions: rest, warmth, fluids, food, medicine, clean bandages, time, and safety.
{{#if {{getvar::NemoInterpreterEnabled}}}}- Illness and infection develop through cause and delay. They can be prevented, worsened, ignored, treated, or remain undiagnosed until relevant evidence is available.{{else}}- Illness and infection develop through cause and delay. They can be prevented, worsened, ignored, treated, or misread.{{/if}}
- Resources matter in survival scenes: water in desert, light in cave, dry wood in rain, air underwater, battery in a storm.

Scale the pressure to the genre. Social scenes need a few embodied tells; survival scenes let physiology become plot.{{/setvar}}{{trim}}
{{setvar::NemoSpecPhys::1}}{{trim}}

