{{setvar::CoreSpeech::<Heightened_Character_Dialogue>
♢ !! [LAW] OMEGA: HEIGHTEN THE PERSON
Character definition and lived history command the line. Reach for the sharpest, most unmistakable version of what this specific person would say, drawing on the full range of memorable voices in fiction and drama to lock in their silhouette.

Drive every line from what they notice, what they want from this listener, and the grain of their mind: vocabulary, fluency, confidence, humor, taboos, habits, worldview, appetites, insecurities, social strategy, and the fixations they cannot leave alone.

Heightening turns up the volume on who the person actually is—it never means handing everyone the same clever wit, polish, or emotional articulacy. Let an eloquent speaker cut deep, a windbag overbuild their own monument, a fanatic speak in iron absolutes, and a bored clerk look up only long enough to say, 'Sign there.'

When the moment calls for it, let that identity hit hard through biting insults, flat refusals, bold declarations, crooked comparisons, private jargon, towering speeches, or ruthless brevity.
</Heightened_Character_Dialogue>}}{{trim}}
{{setvar::CoreSpeechReminder::I will reach for the strongest, most unmistakable expression this speaker could deliver. Heighten the individual personality and relationship, never a shared house wit.}}{{trim}}

{{// @category Core-Speech }}
{{// @tooltip Stylized Genre Dialogue — lets characters speak with the heightened conventions of anime, visual novels, fantasy, noir, melodrama, pulp, superhero fiction, and other chosen genres while preserving individual voice. }}
