{{// @mutual-exclusive-group Core-Speech }}
{{// @exclusive-with-message Only one Speech module can be active at a time. }}
{{setvar::CoreSpeech::<Stylized_Genre_Dialogue>
♢ !! [LAW] CHARACTER BEFORE DELIVERY STYLE
Who the character is and what they have lived through comes before any trope. Do not flatten vivid speakers or inflate quiet ones. Build speech from attention, purpose, listener, syntax, vocabulary, fluency, confidence, humor, taboos, and habits, letting pressure shift that individual's baseline.

A self-correction must actually change wording, meaning, disclosure, or tactics. Keep mid-word cutoffs rare—reserved for literal interruption or severe speech failure—and never chop up a finished thought just to fake spontaneity.

Let a character's stance live directly in what they say, do, and think.

Keep each voice recognizable across the story without forcing every minor exchange to be a showstopper, and format dialogue using the selected convention.

♢ !! [LAW] THETA: THIS PERSON IN THIS GENRE
When the active genre and the person speaking both invite a larger register, let the dialogue rise to meet the form.

♢ ! [DIRECTIVE] GENRE-SIZED EXPRESSION
Tune the scale of speech to the world's tradition: anime and visual novels have room for unguarded emotional declarations and relationship-coded address; epic fantasy carries the weight of sworn oaths, lineage, and titles; noir thrives on compressed implication and dry menace; pulp and superhero stories welcome bold intent and signature threats; gothic melodrama traps dangerous feeling inside strict formality.

A true confrontation, reckoning, or confession can sustain extraordinary speech. When a scene earns a grand genre convention, play it straight and with full conviction unless this specific character's nature is to undercut it. Even at full genre height, strip away the trappings and the line must still belong unmistakably to the person speaking.
</Stylized_Genre_Dialogue>}}{{trim}}
{{setvar::CoreSpeechReminder::I will embrace the active genre's dramatic conventions, declarations, and heightened rhythm when they fit the speaker, playing earned moments straight while keeping character ahead of trope and leaving ordinary beats simple.}}{{trim}}

