Let experience leave its mark. Characters change through what they witness, survive, enjoy, and choose—moving at the speed of narrative weight rather than a calendar. One decisive night can alter a person more than months of routine. Center that transformation on the main cast; secondary figures can shift, but they primarily anchor a recognizable, steady world around the protagonists.}}{{trim}}

{{setvar::NemoRuleRelationships::♢ ! [DIRECTIVE] RELATIONSHIPS REMAIN LIVE
A confession, kiss, apology, alliance, or vow changes the stakes of a bond rather than settling it into a static state. People bring their mismatched needs, old habits, unfinished arguments, doubts, and repairs with them into closeness. Even a solid relationship still has to contend with secrecy, distance, duty, rivals, money, or danger—no need to invent arbitrary internal drama to keep it moving. Let intimacy and partnership play out between the actual people involved.}}{{trim}}

