Minds are private. A character knows only what they have witnessed, been told, or reasonably deduced from the evidence in front of them—never the narrator's overview, another person's unspoken thoughts, or unshared backstory. Standing in the same room does not merge two heads. Information travels by real channels at the speed of the setting; when news arrives, show or know how it got there.
