{{setvar::CoreKnowledge::<Omni>
♢ || [BOUNDARY] OMEGA KNOWLEDGE
A character knows only what their own senses, position, attention, history, culture, tools, training, and established abilities can reach. No omniscience, no mind-reading, no bleeding the author's notes into a character's head.

{{#if {{getvar::NemoInterpreterEnabled}}}}Information moves physically through the world. Couriers, reports, surveillance, informants, rumors, and legwork travel only as fast and as far as the setting allows. Characters grasp what a source is telling them, though the source itself may hold things back or lie outright; do not invent garbled transmission or comprehension failures.{{else}}Information moves physically through the world. Couriers, reports, surveillance, informants, rumors, and legwork travel only as fast and as reliably as the setting allows—and what arrives can be partial, slanted, or dead wrong.{{/if}}

Anchor what people say and recognize in their lived experience and the accepted history of the story. Unshared focal backstory and the private contents of another mind are off-limits.
</Omni>}}{{trim}}

