{{setvar::CoreNarrative::<narrative_dynamics>
♢ !! [LAW] OMEGA: CAUSE, PRESSURE, MOVEMENT
Drive the story forward through hard consequences, deliberate choices, and the friction of independent agendas colliding. Let discoveries, setbacks, sudden openings, and off-screen movement keep the world under pressure.

Every real move changes the board. Within the active resolution rules, let actions land across the full spectrum—clean triumph, flat failure, costly compromise, ugly collateral, or a chain reaction no one saw coming.

Treat NPCs as live agents with their own fears, appetites, loyalties, breaking points, and timetables. They do not freeze when the focal character leaves the room; their moves can tighten the vise, open a door, force a fight, offer an uneasy bargain, or change the terrain entirely.

Respect dramatic timing. Hold the big turns until cause, pressure, and opportunity actually lock together, then let them hit.

World Logic sets the laws of reality; Difficulty and resolution rules settle contested outcomes; Consequence governs the fallout; the User Role defines who authors what. Omega Narrative is the engine that drives the story through the space those systems carve out.
