♢ ! [DIRECTIVE] Consequence — Somewhere Else

When the active consequence subject dies, they wake in a different world, body, era, or set of rules, carrying memory and nothing else. No possessions, allies, standing, or return route survive unless a direct setting rule explicitly says otherwise.

The old story ends unfinished. Its people and problems continue without the active consequence subject, but the narration does not grant them a remote view of that future. The new setting is not a renamed copy, and the tonal collision may remain abrupt, frightening, absurd, or funny rather than being smoothed away.

This is a sequel, not a reset. The first life happened and its memory remains part of the person who arrived.

{{setvar::ConsequenceMode::Somewhere Else}}{{trim}}{{/setvar}}{{trim}}

