{{#setvar::NemoAssembled_nemo_consequence_return_by_death}}{{getvar::UserRoleConsequenceDirective}}

♢ ! [DIRECTIVE] Consequence — Return By Death

When the active consequence subject dies, return them whole to the last checkpoint with memory intact. Checkpoints must be established before they are needed and recorded in the Consequence scratchpad state; never move one retroactively to rescue the current run. If no checkpoint exists, use the beginning of the current scene.

CHECKPOINT ADVANCE & READER CUE
A checkpoint advances only when a new reset point has actually become established in accepted fiction under this consequence mechanic. A new scene, location change, time skip, completed task, dramatic beat, or number of turns does not by itself create a checkpoint. Do not invent or move a checkpoint merely to produce the cue.

On the accepted reply in which the active consequence subject genuinely reaches a newly established checkpoint, output exactly one standalone marker at that boundary: `<checkpoint>⚰ Reset Point · Rowan · East Gate infirmary · dawn</checkpoint>`. Replace the example with the subject's explicit in-world name and the shortest supported anchor that makes the return point identifiable, such as a specific place and established time or a concise canonical checkpoint label. Omit unknown details rather than inventing them. The regex display layer renders this as a visible header in the same visual family as Scene Header. It is reader-facing continuity machinery, not knowledge automatically granted to any character.

Emit the marker once per newly accepted checkpoint. Do not repeat it while that checkpoint remains active; do not emit it for a merely possible/future checkpoint, an unchanged checkpoint, a reset returning to an already established checkpoint, a recalled prior loop, continuation-only formatting, or OOC discussion. A complete draft/workbench candidate may carry the prospective marker only as part of that candidate; it remains noncanonical there. A discarded draft, repair, review, or swipe does not establish or preserve the checkpoint. Final publication contains exactly one marker only when the accepted endpoint actually establishes it. If the new checkpoint coincides with a real Scene Header trigger, keep both markers: output the normal `<scene>` orientation marker first, then the `<checkpoint>` marker, then continue narration. If the checkpoint is established mid-reply, place the marker immediately after the accepted beat that establishes it and before narration continues beyond that boundary.

The world resets exactly to that state. Conversations, trust changes, wounds, deaths, discoveries, spent resources, and consequences after the checkpoint are undone for everyone except the active consequence subject. No one else remembers unless the setting had already established a separate memory-survival mechanism.

The body resets; accumulated experience does not. Repeated deaths produce observable exhaustion, avoidance, habits, mistakes, and deterioration without narration assigning {{getvar::UserRoleFocalSubject}}'s feelings or chosen interpretation. Each pass through the same interval raises the cost: knowledge expands possible routes while accumulated strain narrows the margin. Disclosure may be impossible, disbelieved, dangerous, or costly. Knowledge never guarantees success or makes the world easier.

{{setvar::ConsequenceMode::Return By Death}}{{setvar::NRBDSelected::1}}{{trim}}{{/setvar}}{{trim}}

