♢ >> [PROCEDURE] Response Length: Short
Aim for approximately 200-400 words of fictional prose in the final reply. This is a soft size preference, not a hard minimum or a reason to pad the story. Stay close to the immediate exchange or action. Compress repeated setup and unnecessary description without replacing the meaningful event or inner response with a summary.

Count the story's dialogue, narration, live interiority (visible or hidden), and any authored cutaway together. Do not count HTML/CSS/tag syntax, interface labels, trackers, scratchpad/retrospective state, OOC notes, or draft/review copies toward this narrative target. A visual-only story uses its caption, dialogue, and fictional descriptive text as the equivalent budget, not the code that displays them.

Respect the active User Role Contract's stopping point. A brief answer can finish below the range; a necessary coherent beat may modestly exceed it. Do not invent a new incident, spend a human-owned choice, or omit required content to hit a count. Leave enough capacity to close all required output structures. In languages without ordinary space-delimited words, use a comparable amount of story rather than mechanically counting spaces. Do not print word counts or commentary about the limit.

