{{#setvar::RSShapeText_continuous}}Continuous movement: follow the settled causal sequence closely. Break at meaningful changes of speaker, action, or attention, carrying one passage into the next without an obligatory opening survey or recap.{{/setvar}}
{{#setvar::RSShapeText_exchange}}Exchange-led: where conversation belongs, let its existing turns organize the surface progression. Place action and authorized private experience at the moments they belong; do not invent speech or suppress a necessary silent passage.{{/setvar}}
{{#setvar::RSShapeText_action}}Action-led: where physical activity matters, organize the prose around its actual changes of position, contact, effort, and consequence. Keep the settled choreography intelligible and let speech and private response accompany it naturally.{{/setvar}}
{{#setvar::RSShapeText_experience}}Experience-led: let an eligible focal character's already relevant perception and private response organize the passage, anchored in outward events. Preserve passage ownership, causal timing, information access, and the selected interiority presentation.{{/setvar}}
{{#setvar::RSShapeText_consequence}}Consequence-led: give an established event's actual effect and the immediate response to it prominence. Preserve chronological and causal clarity; do not manufacture a reversal, revelation, or aftermath to supply the structure.{{/setvar}}
{{#setvar::RSShapeText_braided}}Braided movement: interleave outward conduct, speech, and authorized private experience where they interact. Let changes of attention shape the paragraphs, without a compulsory rotation, equal shares, or a repeated dialogue-action-thought template.{{/setvar}}
{{#setvar::RSCadenceText_mixed}}Mixed cadence: vary sentence and passage lengths with speech, causal clarity, and changes of attention; avoid repeating the same sentence openings or paragraph pattern.{{/setvar}}
{{#setvar::RSCadenceText_contrast}}Contrast at real turns: use compact passages at decisive moments and fuller passages where an action or private connection needs development. Emphasis follows actual significance rather than a fixed short-long alternation.{{/setvar}}
{{#setvar::RSCadenceText_connected}}Connected flow: sustain a connected passage while its attention and activity remain continuous, then give a genuine change a concise line or natural break. Preserve readable speaker changes and the selected prose style.{{/setvar}}
