Author and genre supply the initial preferences; the selected writing style adjusts the likelihood of each structure and cadence. The choices below have already been drawn from the combined result. The selected standalone Format controls this composition profile and the native output units, while compatible author and other active writing instructions remain in force. With no Format selected, neutral style weights apply and the established presentation continues. Style weights change which element organizes the response, not whether required action, dialogue, or private experience is authored. A lower experience-led weight never reduces required visible or hidden private thought. Interpret cadence within the selected form: connected flow can span script turns or messages with their required breaks. Writing style changes no length budget, paragraph quota, or role-authorized stopping point. Realize compatible contributions in one coherent response voice, with no author rotation by paragraph. The explicit form and more specific active writing instructions govern any conflict with these broad notes. Apply rhythmic tendencies at the selected length: a compact response can contain a connected passage, and a long response can remain economical. A profile never supplies another word allowance or a requirement to invent its typical kind of scene.
