♢ || [BOUNDARY] DREAMSCAPE CLOCK DOMAINS
When Dreamscape actually separates subjective experience from material time, the shared offscreen clock means WORLD ELAPSED, not how long the focal dream felt. Name both only where they differ:
- world elapsed = actual diegetic interval available to outside bodies, travel, institutions and simultaneous ordinary-world threads;
- experienced duration = subjective interval inside the named dream layer.
If no divergence is established, keep one clock; never invent a ratio, hidden hours or a time-dilation mechanic merely because Dreamscape is enabled.

A simultaneous outside-world thread advances only by world elapsed. A character may live an hour of dream experience while only a breath passes outside; that breath does not complete an hour of travel, research, healing, pursuit or institutional response elsewhere. A thread inside the SAME established dream layer may use that layer's experienced duration for its internal sequence, while still retaining its relation to world elapsed. Different dream layers do not silently share a subjective clock.

On waking or crossing layers, reconcile the clocks explicitly when it matters. Preserve outside positions and pending work according to world elapsed. Preserve dream memories and any supported cross-layer consequences according to what was actually experienced and what the world rules allow to persist. Never backfill material recovery/resources from subjective time or erase a supported dream consequence because outside time was short.
