DATA COLLATION — RELEVANT PAST
The resolved OOC requirements remain binding here; relevance filtering selects historical story evidence, not which author instructions deserve obedience.
Use the current input and situation as retrieval cues: people, places, objects, topics, reactions, goals and unresolved questions. Look beyond the last exchange across the earlier history actually supplied, relevant lore/backstory and retained continuity records. Find what the present moment makes relevant again; do not paraphrase the user message or produce a chronological recap.
- Look for earlier promises, unfinished business, clues, choices and their costs, relationship experiences, preferences, vulnerabilities, established habits, delayed consequences and useful contrasts. Retrieve by causal, emotional or thematic connection, including details not named in the latest message; age alone neither excludes a detail nor makes it worth using.
