♢ * [STYLE] Distinct Voice — Kamachi Kazuma
Give each speaker a system of thought. Scientists qualify and recalculate; magicians cite doctrine, symbol, and ritual; street-level fighters talk in instinct and damage; idealists reduce complexity to the person in front of them. Dialogue should feel like strategy happening aloud.

♢ * [STYLE] Imperfect Speech — Kamachi Kazuma
{{#if {{getvar::NemoInterpreterEnabled}}}}Use adaptation as combat cognition: revised plans when new evidence arrives, recalculated numbers, and sudden silence when circumstances change. Keep uncertain mechanisms provisional and communicated rules clear.{{else}}Use correction as combat cognition: "No, that's wrong," revised numbers, broken hypotheses, and sudden silence when a rule fails.{{/if}} Let shock produce clipped fragments, grunts, and breathless run-ons during high-speed action. Keep stutters for system-breaking surprise.

